1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,692
Seeds split two ways.

2
00:00:01,692 --> 00:00:13,750
In endospermic, or albuminous, seeds the endosperm stays in the mature seed as the food store, and the cotyledons stay thin: maize, wheat, rice, castor and coconut.

3
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:21,041
In cereals, the aleurone layer secretes alpha amylase on germination to digest the starch.

